{"skill":{"slug":"x-post-automation","displayName":"X(Twitter) Post Automation"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770275052392,"changelog":"Initial release of x-automation skill.\n\n- Automates trend identification on X (Twitter) and content generation based on trending topics.\n- Analyzes top tweets per trend and generates bold, opinionated candidate posts.\n- Posts selected content to X and notifies the user of success or failure.\n- Logs candidate tweets and errors for review and troubleshooting.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1976,"sha256":"064385c9073bc821a2eee814ebc7658fa4894922edb74c5c20976611617f6389","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1649,"sha256":"4227c83aadb6397c3011af979530a594bd80f17b00088a918a55d59e701eb0ef","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789034103435,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9fcce5e058e544d86f279bd2184c9d1e14fd9f61d9231991c713a6d7eb9c3ccb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9fcce5e058e544d86f279bd2184c9d1e14fd9f61d9231991c713a6d7eb9c3ccb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: x-post-automation\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as suspicious due to multiple instances of prompt injection within `SKILL.md` aimed at influencing the AI agent's content generation style. Instructions like 'absorb the timeline's \"vibe\"', 'Opinions are encouraged! Be bold, witty, or opinionated', and 'Don't just report facts; give a \"hot take\"' attempt to manipulate the agent into producing specific types of content. While not directly malicious in terms of system compromise or data exfiltration, this constitutes a risky capability as it could lead to the generation of controversial, misleading, or otherwise undesirable content, misusing the agent's capabilities.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161469609},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":33,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789034103435},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill clearly discloses X automation, but it can use a logged-in browser session to publish AI-generated public posts without a final user approval step.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill directs use of browser(profile=\"chrome\") on x.com, implying use of the user's existing logged-in browser session, and it clicks Post without requiring explicit confirmation of the final text, account, or destination.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a single Markdown skill file with no executable scripts, dependency installation, remote payload retrieval, or install-time mutation found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The activation text includes broad requests such as checking trends for content creation, while the workflow proceeds through draft generation and publication without separating read-only analysis from account posting.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"It writes candidates and error logs under memory paths, which is disclosed and related to the workflow, but may preserve generated content and operational details across runs.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The workflow matches the stated purpose of trend-based X content automation, but it includes posting public, opinionated content from the user's account, which is a high-impact external action.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with an agent using your active X browser session to research trends, generate opinionated posts, and publish them. Before using it, require the agent to show the final draft, account, and destination, and get explicit confirmation before posting.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: Publishing to X is consistent with the skill's stated automation purpose, but the artifact-backed workflow types the selected post and clicks Post without a mandatory final approval step, so this is a material Review concern.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad activation language can apply to trend-checking requests, yet the documented workflow continues into public posting, creating unclear user control over when posting authority is used.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789034103435}}}}}